  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full two-hour set at Upstate Concert Hall in Clifton Park, New York, on Saturday, April 21, 2018 [1][2]. This performance is the 257th of 467 archived shows for the band, following a previous recording from April 15, 2018 [3]. The setlist opened with “Michael Myers Resplendent” and “Have To Explode” before moving into “Oceanographer’s Choice” [1][2]. Notable tracks included “How To Embrace A Swamp Creature” and “Moon Over Goldsboro” [1][2]. The band highlighted specific songs with spoken introductions, including “Horshradish Road,” “Night Light,” and “Unicorn Tolerance” [1][2]. A segment featuring John and Matt played “Wear Black,” while John performed “Distant Stations” solo [1][2]. The main set concluded with “Rain in Soho” [1][2]. The encore began with “Liza Forever Minnelli” and “Up the Wolves” [1][2]. Additional encore songs included “Amy AKA Spent Gladiator 1,” “This Year,” and “Southwestern Territory” [1][2]. The final tracks were “No Children” and “Spent Gladiator 2” [1][2]. The recommended recording, taped by torbar, captures all 23 songs in 109 minutes [1][3]. A second recording by natsinator is also available, though it lists zero songs in the metadata [2][3]. Listeners should note that “Horshradish Road” was a bustout, appearing for the first time in 36 archived shows [1][3]. The recording was made from the second row using a Google Pixel phone [1].",
